Game Notes
==========
I never play Barbarians.  Well almost never.  Due to some of the things I
ran into, this deserves a little explanation.

I've never ascended before, but my last two characters have been VERY
close.  Several weeks ago I posted about "This could be it!" about my
Samurai with the good equipment.  He died, choked on a gunyoki.  How
humiliating.  But it was fair, I was pushing it way too much on eating.  I
had a really cool amount of equipment though, holy water out the wazoo,
etc.

My next almost-ascension was a Ranger.  He found my Samurai bones level! 
So after looting the corpse (with the nifty named weapons, etc), he went
on to get all three implements, but I was so excited after getting the
Book finally (never had done it before), I didn't notice I was burdened,
and fell down the stairs and hit myself with a cockatrice corpse.  Another
humiliating death.

It turns out when this Barbarian reached the wizard's tower, he ran into a
statue of remillard.  Now the gems and such were all from this game,
because in the Ranger game, I'd stashed a gem bag at Level 1 so I didn't
get any of the loot, but it was still an interesting coincidence.  

So I played a Barbarian out of pure "need to do something else"
frustration and there you go, my first ascension, but with touching the
other two.  Kinda neat.

Other notes:
The bit about never using Elbereth is true.  Aside from using that as my
usual wand testing inscription, I never used it to save me from anything. 
I didn't really realize it til the end, but it was somewhat interesting.

I really did find three temples of each alignment in 3 subsequent levels. 
It was really strange.  I was very altar heavy this game.  They were all
over the place.

I only got 5 wishes.  I'm not sure if the wand in the castle is guaranteed
to be fully charged or not.  I zapped it once, and got a wish, and then a
Nothing Happened.  I used a wand of enlightenment and my luck was good, so
I tried it again, and still Nothing Happened.  I used a blessed scroll of
charging and got a few more wishes out of it.  I think the record from the
end game is 5 though I sort of count 6 (the first one, 3 subsequent ones,
and then the worn out wand wish, and one from a throne).

Did the Mines first, and then Sokoban, then the Quest.  Had absolutely no
trouble with the Quest at all.  Really simple. 

Potions of Gain Level were smoky.  I had djinni's popping out all over the
place, unfortunately, mostly due to other monsters quaffing them.  I never
got a djinni or a wish out of one of my potions.

I was really identify scroll and holy water short the entire game til the
end.  I didn't know I had a genocide scroll til after the Castle.  That's
when the Liches went.  The throne in the Castle game me another genocide
and there went the master mind flayers.

Gehennom was pretty easy, though I had a helluva time finding Vlad's
Tower.  I literally destroyed about 10 levels of dungeon with a pick axe
until I found the one spot where my sight hadn't extended and found it. 
Vlad was pretty easy.

The Moloch's sanctum fight wasn't too bad.  

The hardest was probably the Astral plane.  I had 403 HP, but I was down
to 200 or so on gaining the altar room.  I was at 150 by the next door. 
If it hadn't been the right altar, I wouldn't have made it.  There really
wasn't much I could do.  I just kept using my wand of death and
progressing a square and weaselling left and right.  It was pretty insane.

